  "verseCount": 16,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Elihu spake moreover, and said,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Thinkest thou this to be right, that thou saidst, My righteousness is more than God’s?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For thou saidst, What advantage will it be unto thee? and, What profit shall I have, if I be cleansed from my sin?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "I will answer thee, and thy companions with thee.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Look unto the heavens, and see; and behold the clouds which are higher than thou.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "If thou sinnest, what doest thou against him? or if thy transgressions be multiplied, what doest thou unto him?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "If thou be righteous, what givest thou him? or what receiveth he of thine hand?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Thy wickedness may hurt a man as thou art; and thy righteousness may profit the son of man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "By reason of the multitude of oppressions they make the oppressed to cry: they cry out by reason of the arm of the mighty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "But none saith, Where is God my maker, who giveth songs in the night;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Who teacheth us more than the beasts of the earth, and maketh us wiser than the fowls of heaven?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "There they cry, but none giveth answer, because of the pride of evil men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "Surely God will not hear vanity, neither will the Almighty regard it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Although thou sayest thou shalt not see him, yet judgment is before him; therefore trust thou in him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "But now, because it is not so, he hath visited in his anger; yet he knoweth it not in great extremity:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:35:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Therefore doth Job open his mouth in vain; he multiplieth words without knowledge.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 35:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:35:16"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
